    "hero": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-hero",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "The flush isn’t the problem. What happens after it is.",
        "as_h1": true,
        "standfirst": "Redness that outlasts its trigger works differently from a blush. The difference isn’t severity — it’s structural.",
        "lead": "<p><strong>You’ve been told it’s a trigger problem.</strong> So you cut the wine, the heat, the long hot showers.</p><p>And it still stays. Through the meeting. Through the drive home. Into the evening.</p><p>One woman put it plainly: <em>“background redness that just won’t go away, no matter what I do.”</em></p><p>That part — the staying — isn’t what the trigger lists are about.</p>",
        "image_alt": "An empty desk beside an office window in late afternoon light",
        "placeholder_note": "[ HERO ]Empty desk beside an office window, late afternoon, cold light from the left. Cardigan over the chair back, chair turned toward the glass. No face, no product. See PRELANDER_VISUAL_BRIEF.md §2.",
        "caption": "<p>The window seat is one of the most commonly reported adaptations. <em>Photograph posed by a model.</em></p>",
        "padding_top": 28,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "meta1": {
          "type": "meta",
          "settings": {
            "text": "The Skin File editorial desk",
            "strong": true
          }
        },
        "meta3": {
          "type": "meta",
          "settings": {
            "text": "25 August 2026",
            "strong": false
          }
        },
        "meta5": {
          "type": "meta",
          "settings": {
            "text": "3 min read",
            "strong": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "meta1",
        "meta3",
        "meta5"
      ]
    },
    "body1": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-block",
      "settings": {
        "rnum": "",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "It isn’t that you flush harder",
        "anchor_id": "",
        "container": "measure",
        "top_rule": false,
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>The usual explanation is that some people simply flush harder. It’s why the advice is always a longer list of triggers.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>It doesn’t hold up.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>People whose flush fades and people whose flush stays react to the same things. Heat. Wine. A hard question in a meeting.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph4": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>What differs is what happens next.</b></p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph5": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>In a face that settles, one system opens the vessels and another closes them. In one that doesn’t, that second half is delayed — or overridden.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph6": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Overridden by what? Trigger lists never say.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph1",
        "paragraph2",
        "paragraph3",
        "paragraph4",
        "paragraph5",
        "paragraph6"
      ]
    },
    "body2": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-block",
      "settings": {
        "rnum": "",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "It behaves less like a symptom than a circuit",
        "anchor_id": "",
        "container": "measure",
        "top_rule": false,
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Dermatology has moved toward describing lasting flushing as a loop, not an event.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "diagram2": {
          "type": "diagram",
          "settings": {
            "which": "loop",
            "aria_label": "Five points arranged in a loop; each lowers the threshold of the next; the fifth is hidden",
            "narrow": true,
            "legend": "<p><b>1</b> Vessel tone — how fully vessels close again. <b>2</b> Nerve signal — the threshold to react at all. <b>3</b> Inflammation — more inputs start it than stop it. <b>4</b> Barrier — when thin, it exposes the nerves beneath. <b>5</b> — not on the skin. It comes later.</p>",
            "caption": ""
          }
        },
        "paragraph3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>Each point lowers the threshold of the next.</b> Treat one and leave four, and the four pull the treated one back.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph4": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>There’s a fifth. It rarely shows up in a treatment plan. It’s the reason the other four keep resetting.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph1",
        "diagram2",
        "paragraph3",
        "paragraph4"
      ]
    },
    "body3": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-block",
      "settings": {
        "rnum": "",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "Why one at a time produces the pattern you know",
        "anchor_id": "",
        "container": "measure",
        "top_rule": false,
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Almost every treatment addresses one point, and does it well. A barrier cream does barrier work. A laser does vessel work. A prescription calms inflammation.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Each leaves the other four exactly where it found them.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Read enough accounts and the same lines repeat:</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "said4": {
          "type": "said",
          "settings": {
            "lines": "“It worked, then it just stopped.”\n“What helps one week does nothing the next.”\n“I’ve spent thousands — lasers, derm visits, monthly meds.”"
          }
        },
        "paragraph5": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Read as personal failures, that history is crushing. Read as a loop, it’s just arithmetic.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "pull6": {
          "type": "pull",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>“It works, then it stops working” sounds like bad luck. In a five-point loop, it’s the expected result.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph1",
        "paragraph2",
        "paragraph3",
        "said4",
        "paragraph5",
        "pull6"
      ]
    },
    "quiz1": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-quiz-cta",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Interactive",
        "heading": "Which of the five points are active on your skin?",
        "body": "A 60-second check built on the five-point framework. It maps your triggers and timing to each one.",
        "button_label": "Find my flush profile →",
        "button_url": "/pages/quiz-flusher?src=v4-tool1",
        "fine_print": "About 60 seconds. No email or account required.",
        "full_width": false,
        "container": "measure",
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      }
    },
    "body4": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-block",
      "settings": {
        "rnum": "",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "The fifth point isn’t on your skin",
        "anchor_id": "",
        "container": "measure",
        "top_rule": false,
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Four of the five you could measure. The fifth you can’t — which is why it’s usually left out.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>Expecting a flush produces the same vascular response as the flush itself.</b></p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Learn to brace for it, and you hand the loop a live signal. Continuously. Even in rooms that aren’t warm.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph4": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>One account says it best: <em>“even when the room isn’t warm, I get so anxious about flushing that it happens.”</em></p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph5": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>It arrives <em>before</em> the trigger. Not imagined — predicted. And the prediction is itself the input.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph6": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>There’s no cream for anticipation.</b> So the useful question isn’t what to apply. It’s which of the five is doing the most work. That differs for every face.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "paragraph1",
        "paragraph2",
        "paragraph3",
        "paragraph4",
        "paragraph5",
        "paragraph6"
      ]
    },
    "quiz2": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-quiz-cta",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Interactive",
        "heading": "Find which point is driving the others",
        "body": "Your five-point profile in 60 seconds — including whether the fifth one is active for you.",
        "button_label": "Find my flush profile →",
        "button_url": "/pages/quiz-flusher?src=v4-tool2",
        "fine_print": "About 60 seconds. No email or account required.",
        "full_width": false,
        "container": "measure",
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      }
    },
    "body5": {
      "type": "rosalia-funnel-block",
      "settings": {
        "rnum": "",
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "What this doesn’t cover",
        "anchor_id": "",
        "container": "measure",
        "top_rule": false,
        "padding_top": 8,
        "padding_bottom": 8,
        "background": "#FAF5F0",
        "text_color": "#2B2620"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "paragraph1": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Two things sit outside all of this, and both matter.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph2": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>Your eyes.</b> Burning, watering or blurring eyes point to ocular rosacea. That’s for an eye doctor — no cream reaches it, and waiting carries real risk.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "paragraph3": {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p><b>Steroid rebound.</b> Redness that started after long steroid use follows a different course. Stopping suddenly is usually worse than the flare, and it needs a doctor’s supervision.</p>",
            "is_lead": false
          }
        },
        "tags4": {
          "type": "tags",
